# Security and tenancy

Single Postgres. Row-level security on every user-owned table. **The policy, not the query, is the boundary.** No application code path may read across accounts.

## Isolation (from mock — lock)

| Object | Policy |
|--------|--------|
| `users` | self-read; platform_admin read via elevated role |
| `portfolios` / `holdings` | owner only; **not** readable by admins unless a support-access grant row exists |
| `analysis_requests` / `reports` | owner only; **metadata** visible to admin (ticker, status, cost — not sections jsonb) |
| `analysis_feedback` | family insert/select own row; **platform_admin** select all (email, ticker, scores, comment — not `reports.sections` or lots) |
| `usage_events` / invoices | owner read; **service-role write only** |
| `prompt_versions` / `audit_log` | admin only; append-only; no delete grant |

Platform admin **logs in at `/admin/login`**, not `/login` (D27). Desk sessions never satisfy admin RLS. Admin sessions cannot `thesis_accept_analysis` or write `holding_lots`.

Impersonation is **read-only**. Every session writes `audit_log` with admin identity, target account, start and end time.

Observability (`observability_*`) is readable by `platform_admin` only. Capture may insert events for the caller’s family. Never store prompt body, report sections, or lots. See [`platform-admin.mdc`](platform-admin.mdc).

## Secrets

- Anon key in the browser. Service role and DB password only in server env / `tools/db`.
- Never commit `readme.rtf`, `.env`, or paste keys into `HANDOFF.md`.
- Signed URLs for PDFs in object storage, keyed by `reports.id`.

## Prompt

System prompt is never in API responses, streamed tokens, or error payloads. See [`investment-framework.mdc`](investment-framework.mdc).

## Anti-patterns

- Using `service_role` in `apps/web` client components
- `auth.uid()` policies that compare the wrong column (`users.id` vs `auth.users.id` must be documented in the migration)
- Admin "View as" that can POST /analysis or PATCH holdings
- Putting Admin console on the research-desk sidebar because the mock HTML did
- Using a desk JWT to open `/admin/observability`
